      "markdown": "## SOME FACTS\n\n1. There are 360 million people who speak English as a first language. 1.5 billion people worldwide speak it as a second or additional language. The British Council claims that 25 per cent of the world's population has some understanding of English.\n\n2. Approximately 3 million new books written in English are published annually.\n\n3. 55% of the internet is in English. The second most popular internet language is Russian at just under 6%.\n\n4. In South Africa the best predictor of university success regardless of field of study is the matric English mark.",
